# HallPass Demo Outline for the Final Pitch

## 1. Opening Problem — 30 seconds

New, international, and exchange students often make important campus-life decisions using information scattered across social media, chat groups, and word of mouth. Comparing dorms, finding affordable food, and understanding daily services takes time and can leave students uncertain.

**Opening question:** “How many different chats or posts should a new student need just to make one confident campus decision?”

## 2. Target User — 20 seconds

- First-year, international, and exchange students at RSU
- Current students who browse or contribute useful experiences
- Administrators who moderate demonstration content and review activity

## 3. Product Solution — 30 seconds

HallPass combines:

- dormitory and cafeteria review browsing;
- keyword search and minimum-rating filters;
- detailed student-focused listings;
- a practical campus survival guide;
- consent-based review submission and status tracking; and
- administrator moderation, reports, users, and audit activity.

The current version is a frontend-only classroom MVP using fictional data, simulated accounts, and browser `localStorage`.

