## 5. Evidence — 45 seconds

### Customer discovery

- The project documentation identifies uncertainty around accommodation, cafeteria choices, and daily campus guidance for new RSU students.
- HallPass responds with one student-focused, searchable interface instead of scattered sources.

### Validation and testing

- Earlier project validation focused on finding dorm/cafeteria reviews, viewing detail, accessing guidance, contributing a review, and understanding the flow.
- Lab 13 testing should measure unassisted task completion, confusion points, privacy comprehension, status comprehension, and recommended fixes.
- Testing results and evidence belong to the team’s separate Lab 13 user-testing deliverables (GitHub Issue #65).

### Product and startup metrics

- Review search/filter use
- Detail views and guide-topic views
- Review submissions and completion rate
- Pending-to-approved/rejected moderation outcomes
- Task success rate and confusion count
- Return intent or willingness to recommend

Do not present planned metrics as live production analytics unless supporting data exists.

## 6. Requirement and Risk Message — 30 seconds

The scripted demo maps every major screen to `docs/system-requirements.md`. HallPass demonstrates the full concept but does not yet include a production backend, secure authentication, server-side authorization, a live database, cloud sync, permanent image storage, or verified institutional content. These boundaries are disclosed so the MVP is evaluated honestly.

## 7. Closing Value Message — 20 seconds

“HallPass helps new RSU students spend less time searching and make more confident campus decisions. It combines student experiences, practical guidance, responsible contribution, and moderation in one clear pathway. Our next step is to use Lab 13 feedback to fix the most important usability issues before the Lab 14 release.”

**Call to action:** Try one browse task and one contribution task, then tell us where the experience should be clearer.
